# No Git LFS here, deliberately.
#
# This site is served by GitHub Pages, and Pages does not resolve LFS objects:
# it returns the pointer file as the response body, so every song becomes a
# 132-byte text file and playback breaks. The audio is committed as ordinary
# binary instead.
#
# There used to be a `*.mp3 filter=lfs` rule here. It looked harmless only
# because git-lfs isn't installed on the machine this repo is usually edited
# from. The first commit made from a machine that *does* have git-lfs (a GitHub
# Actions runner, during a Suno playlist sync) silently rewrote every track to
# a pointer and took the between-innings player down. Don't reintroduce it.
